$DATUM [[2-(Hydroxymethyl)-4-nitrophenyl]thio]acetic acid (21) To a stirred
solution of 9.38 g 2-chloro-5-nitrobenzyl alcohol (20, 0.05 mol) and 20.9
cm3 triethylamine (0.15 mol) in 25 cm3 DMSO was added 3.55 cm3
thioglycolic acid (0.05 mol). After being stirred at 50 °C for 5 h, the
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, quenched with 250 cm3
water, and acidified with HCl to pH = 5. The precipitate was filtered
off, washed with water, and solubilized in aqueous solution of NaOH.
Then, the solution was stirred with activated carbon, filtered, and
acidified with HCl to pH = 5. The precipitate was filtered, washed with
water, and dried. White solid; yield 74 %; m.p.: 139–140 °C (H2O); 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6, 400 MHz): δ = 8.27 (s, 1H, H-3), 8.04 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H, H-5),
7.45 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H, H-6), 5.55 (br s, 1H, OH), 4.53 (s, 2H, CH2-O),
3.93 (s, 2H, CH2-S) ppm; 13C NMR (DMSO-d6, 100 MHz): δ = 169.9, 144.8,
143.5, 130.3, 125.5, 122.1, 120.2, 59.7, 33.7 ppm; IR (KBr): ν = 3371
(OH), 1720 (CO), 1526 (NO2), 1343 (NO2) cm-1. C9H9NO5S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel synthesis of 2H-1,5-benzoxathiepin-3(4H)-one and
5H-4,1-benzoxathiepin-3(2H)-one derivatives and chemical properties
